reviewNotes:
Substrate Workouts works on its own on the device, with a sample routine; signing in to Substrate, a personal server its user runs, keeps the training there. We run a demonstration server for review with no real user's data.

To sign in:
1. Open the app and tap Sign In to Your Substrate… at the bottom of Routines. Under Repository or server, enter {server} and tap Continue.
2. Tap Sign In with Your Substrate.
3. On the server's Sign in to your Substrate page, enter the repository and password below and tap Sign in.
4. Scroll down and tap Approve and set up (Approve, once the app is set up). The app returns signed in.

Repository: {user}
Password: {password}

Then start an empty session from Routines, add an exercise and log a set. HealthKit is used to save each finished session as a strength workout and to read body mass for suggestions; Health data is never used for advertising and goes only to the user's own server. Accounts live on the user's own server and are never created in the app. Privacy policy: {privacy}
